.5. Road closed expect delays due to safety concerns. Comment: Due to forecasted winter weather, the Colorado Department of Transportation, in partnership with the Colorado Avalanche Information Center, will close Colorado Highway 82 over Independence Pass between Aspen and Twin Lakes beginning at 8 a.m. on Saturday, October 31. The incoming storm is expected to bring snow accumulation and strong winds, making travel across the high-mountain pass hazardous. Conditions will be re-evaluated once the storms pass to determine whether the road can reopen for the fall or will enter its annual winter shutdown. CO 82 will be closed at approximately Lincoln Creek Road (Mile Point 51.1) on the west side and near Graham Gulch (MP 68.5) on the east side. The alternate route from the Denver Metro Area to Aspen is via westbound I-70 to Glenwood Springs, then CO 82 to Aspen.","impact":"minor","roads":"CO-82E","lat":39.120485,"lon":-106.686391,"chain_law":false,"closure":true,"pass_relevant":true,"observed":"2026-11-05T23:59:16.956Z","start_time":"2026-10-29T21:49:45.146Z","clear_time":null,"category":"Traffic","severity":"minor","source":"incident","geometry_kind":"point","distance_km":26.7},{"id":"OpenTMS-Event36209288665","title":"Paving Operations-152018","type":"Paving Operations","description":"Between Exit 133: Dotsero (near Gypsum) and US 6 (near Eagle) from Mile Point 139 to Mile Point 147. Right lane closed due to paving operations. Width limit in effect. Width limit 11'0\". Starting Sunday at 7:00AM MST until Sunday, at about 7:00PM MST. Full schedule below: • November 8, 7:00AM - November 8, 7:00PM Comment: Eastbound and westbound Eagle (Exit 147) and Gypsum (Exit 140) on/off ramp lane shifts, intermittent single lane closures, speed reduced to 55 mph and 10-20 minute delays. For more information email: resurfacingproject@gmail.com.","impact":null,"roads":"I-70E","lat":39.653831,"lon":-106.964908,"chain_law":false,"closure":true,"pass_relevant":false,"observed":"2026-11